[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m ### Step 2: Use coordinate geometry
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m Let’s place the triangle in the coordinate plane.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m Let’s place the triangle such that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m - The circumcenter $O$ is at the origin $(0, 0)$,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m - The incenter $I$ is at some point $(x, y)$,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m - The vector $\vec{OI} = (x, y)$,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m - The vector $\vec{IA} = (x_A - x, y_A - y)$, where $A = (x_A, y_A)$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m We are told that $\vec{IA} \perp \vec{OI}$, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m (x_A - x)(x) + (y_A - y)(y) = 0
