[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m We know $OI^2 = 13$, and $AO = R = 13$, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m IA^2 + 13 = 169 \Rightarrow IA^2 = 156
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m IA = \sqrt{156} = 2\sqrt{39}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m Now, we can use the formula for the distance from the incenter to a vertex:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m IA^2 = R^2 - \left( \frac{r}{\sin \frac{A}{2}} \right)^2
