[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m In a rhombus:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m - All sides are equal in length.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m - The diagonals bisect each other at right angles (but not necessarily perpendicular unless it's a square).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m - The diagonals intersect at the origin, so the origin is the midpoint of both diagonals.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m Let the diagonals be $AC$ and $BD$, and let their intersection be the origin.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m Let the coordinates of the vertices be:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25208)[0m - $A = (a, b)$
